/STR 5d70d316
Toledo is full of alleys and all you want is the rest of the story.
/STR 47f2fb59
You reread Belianis of Greece for the umpteenth time. The wounds he gave and received still seem too many to you.
/STR a33f2ba2
"Sovereign and exalted lady..." How well you write when you put your mind to it.
/STR ff70ae6e
There are hundreds. You couldn't carry them and, besides, why bother, when you know them by heart?
/STR 11135c4a
Amadis of Gaul, The Exploits of Esplandian, Belianis of Greece, Palmerin of Oliva, Tirant lo Blanc... Everything a gentleman needs to lose his wits.
/STR 07b4aff7
You tear the pasteboard covers off a book by Feliciano de Silva. Nobody will miss it.
/STR f8772534
A wall rack, the kind for hanging lances. That's what it's for.
/STR 61b91b65
A smooth wall, freshly whitewashed, just where the door of your library used to be. It smells of lime and enchantment.
/STR caa3ca01
